## 4. Joining strings

| Method                               | Purpose                                          |
| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |
| `joining()`                          | Join strings without a delimiter                 |
| `joining(delimiter)`                 | Join strings using a delimiter                   |
| `joining(delimiter, prefix, suffix)` | Join strings with a delimiter, prefix and suffix |

Example:

```
List<String> names = Arrays.asList("Ravi", "Priya", "Arun");

String result = names.stream()
    .collect(Collectors.joining(", ", "[", "]"));

System.out.println(result);

// [Ravi, Priya, Arun]
```

## 5. Mapping, filtering and flattening

| Method                             | Purpose                                             | Introduced |
| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
| `mapping(mapper, downstream)`      | Transform elements before downstream collection     | Java 8     |
| `filtering(predicate, downstream)` | Filter within a downstream collector                | Java 9     |
| `flatMapping(mapper, downstream)`  | Flatten nested streams before downstream collection | Java 9     |

