## 7. Finishing and combining collectors

| Method                                    | Purpose                                      | Introduced |
| ----------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
| `collectingAndThen(downstream, finisher)` | Transform the final collection result        | Java 8     |
| `teeing(collector1, collector2, merger)`  | Run two collectors and combine their results | Java 12    |

## 8. Concurrent collection methods

These are particularly useful when working with parallel streams and concurrent maps.

| Method                                                                | Purpose                                                 |
| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `toConcurrentMap(keyMapper, valueMapper)`                             | Collect into a concurrent map                           |
| `toConcurrentMap(keyMapper, valueMapper, mergeFunction)`              | Resolve duplicate keys                                  |
| `toConcurrentMap(keyMapper, valueMapper, mergeFunction, mapSupplier)` | Choose the concurrent map implementation                |
| `groupingByConcurrent(classifier)`                                    | Group elements concurrently                             |
| `groupingByConcurrent(classifier, downstream)`                        | Concurrent grouping with a downstream collector         |
| `groupingByConcurrent(classifier, mapFactory, downstream)`            | Concurrent grouping with a specified map implementation |
